{"id": "EUVD-2026-86130", "enisaUuid": "7628b706-1b9c-3b17-bc17-879359703800", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: do not use make_bad_inode() in ocfs2_read_inode_block_full()\n\nThis reverts commit 58b6fcd2ab34 (\"ocfs2: mark inode bad upon validation\nfailure during read\").\n\nSince 'make_bad_inode()' resets inode type to S_IFREG, doing this for\ndirectory inode during active VFS lookup is likely to confuse the latter,\nincluding VFS_BUG_ON_INODE() triggered in this case.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:51:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e7459abff46e28e64367057038ef8607e63f599", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d48ace65322001b41bb5322442a21425ef4407d4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93258", "GHSA-xg3j-cr9w-jr78"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c2cb3ac-0afc-3223-95e3-3b195bfebfa5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "596d9eff-b178-3bbf-99b3-bd216d50a2f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "6e9e4934-ac69-3caf-b6df-ba02cb558623", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7575b4d7-1232-39aa-8450-6819ca1e6664", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "58b6fcd2ab34399258dc509f701d0986a8e0bcaa <0e7459abff46e28e64367057038ef8607e63f599"}, {"id": "7687953d-0b83-3bc5-b9d1-cdc66143c8c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8cd0cc27-4444-3361-8372-9556f6e4c64e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "58b6fcd2ab34399258dc509f701d0986a8e0bcaa <d48ace65322001b41bb5322442a21425ef4407d4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cc17c569-2589-35fa-99e0-788f1efaa9fd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited"